course: dictionary
lesson: 12796
title: Eldest and the oldest in the family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Eldest means oldest, and we use it for people in the same family. «My eldest brother is twelve.» This tells you that out of all the brothers in the family, he is the oldest.
explain: Old, older and oldest go up in steps. «Tom is old. Sam is older than Tom. Ben is the oldest of the three.» Eldest means the same as oldest, and it is most often used for brothers, sisters and children in a family.
explain: The eldest can also stand alone as a name for a person. «The eldest is in Year 6.» Here the eldest means the oldest child in the family. Use «the eldest» when you are talking about one person, and use «eldest» before a noun, as in «eldest sister».
fact: Eldest means oldest, used for people in the same family.
fact: «The eldest son» means the oldest boy in the family.
fact: «Eldest of three» means the oldest out of three people.
fact: The eldest is the oldest child in a family.
fact: Eldest is the superlative of old, like oldest, and it is used mostly when talking about family.
exercise: «My eldest sister is studying at university.» What does eldest mean here? | Newest | Youngest | *Oldest | Tallest
exercise: Sam is 8, Leo is 11 and Max is 6. They are three brothers. Who is the eldest? | *Leo | Sam | Max
exercise: Find and copy the word that means oldest in this sentence: «Anya is the eldest of three girls.» | three | Anya | girls | *eldest
test: «The eldest child in our family is nine.» What is the eldest? | *The oldest child in the family | A teacher | A child | The youngest child
test: Which word is the superlative of old, used for family? | Youngest | Olden | *Eldest | Older
exam: «Jack is the eldest of the four cousins.» What does this tell you about Jack? | He is the newest | He is the youngest | *He is the oldest of the four | He is the shortest
